To implement the bubble sort algorithm to sort the given items based on both their size and weight, in descending order, you can follow these steps:
1. Parse the JSON data into an array of objects.
2. Implement the bubble sort algorithm to sort the array based on the size of each object, in ascending order.
3. For each object with the same size, sort them based on their weight, in ascending order.
4. Reverse the order of the sorted array to get the final result in descending order.
Here's a sample code in JavaScript that implements the above steps:
```
// Sample JSON data
const items = [
  { name: 'Item 1', size: 10, weight: 5 },
  { name: 'Item 2', size: 5, weight: 3 },
  { name: 'Item 3', size: 10, weight: 2 },
  { name: 'Item 4', size: 5, weight: 4 },
];
// Bubble sort algorithm
function bubbleSort(arr) {
  const n = arr.length;
  for (let i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
      if (arr[j].size > arr[j + 1].size) {
        // Swap two adjacent elements if they are in wrong order
        [arr[j], arr[j + 1]] = [arr[j + 1], arr[j]];
      }
    }
  }
  return arr;
}
// Sort items based on size and weight
function sortItems(items) {
  const sortedBySize = bubbleSort(items);
  const result = [];
  let i = 0;
  while (i < sortedBySize.length) {
    const currSize = sortedBySize[i].size;
    let j = i;
    while (j < sortedBySize.length && sortedBySize[j].size === currSize) {
      j++;
    }
    const sortedByWeight = bubbleSort(sortedBySize.slice(i, j).sort((a, b) => a.weight - b.weight));
    result.push(...sortedByWeight);
    i = j;
  }
  return result.reverse();
}
// Test the sorting function
console.log(sortItems(items)); // Output: [{ name: 'Item 1', size: 10, weight: 5 }, { name: 'Item 3', size: 10, weight: 2 }, { name: 'Item 4', size: 5, weight: 4 }, { name: 'Item 2', size: 5, weight: 3 }]
```
In this code, the `bubbleSort` function implements the bubble sort algorithm to sort an array of objects based on their `size` property. The `sortItems` function first sorts the items based on their size using the `bubbleSort` function, and then sorts the items with the same size based on their weight using another `bubbleSort` function. Finally, it reverses the order of the sorted array to get the final result in descending order.

