        for (int i = SEQ_CHARS.length(); i < passwordLength; i++) {
            int randomIndex = random.nextInt(PASSWORD_ALLOW_BASE.length());
            passwordBuilder.append(PASSWORD_ALLOW_BASE.charAt(randomIndex));
        }
        // Shuffle characters
        char[] passwordChars = passwordBuilder.toString().toCharArray();
        for (int i = 0; i < passwordLength; i++) {
            int randomIndex = random.nextInt(passwordLength);
            char temp = passwordChars[i];
            passwordChars[i] = passwordChars[randomIndex];
            passwordChars[randomIndex] = temp;
        }
        return new String(passwordChars);
    }
}
```
The `generatePassword` method first adds the sequence characters to the password, then adds random characters from the allowed character set until the password reaches the desired length. Finally, it shuffles the characters randomly to increase security.

